Prevention of hydrogen embrittlement in steels — Bhadeshia (@mat-hydrogen-source: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mat-sources) { r_1VT41JGPGJ3NGXT47VKG1DFCT4
H. K. D. H. Bhadeshia, *Prevention of Hydrogen Embrittlement in Steels*, ISIJ International 56 (2016), 24–36. [Author's publication page](https://www.phase-trans.msm.cam.ac.uk/2016/prevention.html), [author-hosted manuscript](https://www.phase-trans.msm.cam.ac.uk/2016/preventing_hydrogen.pdf).

Read the complete review and trace the experimental evidence for entry barriers, processing, transport and trapping. Title, introduction and selected hydrogen-trapping discussion were inspected on 30 October 2026. The review advances a prevention-focused interpretation: assess its claims against the particular trap, loading, temperature and exposure timescale rather than treating total absorbed hydrogen as a sufficient measure of susceptibility.

Freely readable author-hosted manuscript; a blanket adaptation licence was not established. Retain citations and external media. This review supports the materials account without replacing the deeper hydrogen-system, welding and fracture subjects.

